format 1

# pklith's own registry: every tracked file type and the hk steps (hk.pkl)
# that check it. `pkli check` judges this repository against it.
#
# Most checks come from pkli's built-in catalog (src/catalog/builtin.pklith).
# The rows below are the ones this repository adds, plus clippy and
# shellcheck, which it overrides: clippy's failure names the §C code limits,
# and shellcheck also reads the extension-less hooks in .githooks/. `pkli
# gen` renders every named check into hk.pklith.pkl.

## checks
id|category|nix|glob|check|fix|env|msg
no-large-files|hygiene|-|**/*|scripts/no-large-files.sh {{files}}|-|-|file over its type's size limit
clippy|lint|clippy|**/*.rs, Cargo.toml, clippy.toml|cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -q -- -D warnings|-|-|clippy finding or a §C code limit exceeded
test|test|cargo-nextest|**/*.rs, Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, src/catalog/builtin.pklith|cargo nextest run --workspace --no-fail-fast --status-level fail --final-status-level fail|-|-|a test failed, or the suite is empty
doctest|test|cargo|**/*.rs, Cargo.toml|cargo test --doc -q|-|-|a doc example failed
rustdoc|lint|cargo|**/*.rs, Cargo.toml|cargo doc --workspace --no-deps --document-private-items -q|-|RUSTDOCFLAGS=-D warnings|docs do not build cleanly
coverage|coverage|sherd|**/*.rs, Cargo.toml, .coverage|sherd coverage --check|-|-|line coverage fell below .coverage
file-ceilings|spec|sherd|**/*.rs|scripts/file-ceilings.sh|-|-|a Rust file is over its token ceiling
shellcheck|lint|shellcheck|.githooks/*, .envrc, **/*.sh|shellcheck --shell=bash {{files}}|-|-|shell script finding
links|lint|lychee|**/*.md|git ls-files -z '*.md' \| xargs -0 lychee --offline --no-progress --include-fragments|-|-|a relative link or anchor is broken
flake-lock-graph|supply|jq|flake.lock|scripts/flake-lock-graph.sh {{files}}|-|-|flake.lock grew a second nixpkgs or too many nodes
deny|supply|cargo-deny|Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, deny.toml|cargo deny check --disable-fetch licenses bans|-|-|a license or ban rule failed
catalog-nix|supply|nix|src/catalog/builtin.pklith, flake.nix, flake.lock, scripts/catalog-nix.sh|scripts/catalog-nix.sh src/catalog/builtin.pklith|-|-|a built-in catalog row names a nix attribute that does not build, or whose binaries its command never calls
agents-table|spec|-|hk.pkl, hk.pklith.pkl, AGENTS.md, dev/**|cargo run -q -p pklith-dev -- agents --check|cargo run -q -p pklith-dev -- agents|-|AGENTS.md step table is stale
gen-check|gate|cargo|-|cargo run -q --bin pkli -- gen --check|-|-|a step in hk.pklith.pkl no longer matches .pklith; run `pkli gen`
pkli-check|gate|cargo|-|cargo run -q --bin pkli -- check|-|-|a tracked file type has no row in .pklith, or a row matches nothing

## types
type|checks|min|exempt
*|trailing-whitespace,final-newline,line-endings,no-bom,no-merge-conflict,no-case-conflict,no-broken-symlinks,no-large-files,no-private-key,ripsecrets,typos|-|-
rs|rustfmt,clippy,test,doctest,rustdoc,coverage,file-ceilings|-|-
nix|nixfmt|-|-
lock|flake-lock-graph|-|-
Cargo.lock|deny|-|-
toml|taplo|-|-
SPEC.md|mth-fmt,mth-check,sherd-check,sherd-nav,sherd-budget,links|-|-
md|links|-|-
sh|shellcheck|-|-
envrc|shellcheck|-|-
pre-commit|shellcheck|-|-
commit-msg|shellcheck|-|-
pre-push|shellcheck|-|-
yml|actionlint,zizmor|-|-
context-limits|sherd-budget|-|-
coverage|coverage|-|-
pkl|-|-|evaluated by the hk-parity step in hk.pkl with both pkl and hk's pklr, against the vendored schema; pkl/Config.pkl is vendored
gitignore|-|-|git configuration; hygiene steps only
LICENSE|-|-|license text, nothing to lint
path:pkl/**|-|-|vendored hk schema and its provenance note; the fixers and ripsecrets skip pkl/ (V7), hk-parity evaluates the schema
path:FORMAT*.md|-|-|vendored verbatim from microlith; the fixers skip it (V7)
pklith|pkli-check,gen-check|-|-
path:src/catalog/builtin.pklith|test,catalog-nix|-|-
